{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat collab/1793530000000-engineer-module-pins.prompt.md'","aggregated_output":"Created-GMT: 2026-10-17 04:00:00 GMT\nCreated-Local: 2026-10-17 11:00:00 +07\nCoding-Agent: codex\nSession-ID: pending (provider-generated)\n# Task: module-identity pins on the row carrier + receiver-side re-check + carried install children admitted by the receiver (Architect threat model verdict \"C\" + R4), uncommitted\nRole: VM Runtime\nImplementers:\n- Model: gpt-6.1-sol | Assigned: 2026-10-17 11:00 +07 | Status: active | Rationale: owner said \"dispatch it to codex\"; Architect (Fable) reviews before any commit; this is a security-relevant format change\n\nWorktree /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-pins (branch srvm-module-pins @ origin/master). Read COMPLETELY: ./collab/*architect-fetch-threat-model.report.md (the Architect's threat model; sections 3 (routes R1-R13), 4.1-4.5, 5, 6 verdict, 7 tests and docs) and ./collab/1793430000000-architect-gap-list.report.md row on Q5. IMPLEMENT the verdict: (1) CARRIER: the task row's `requires` carries `:yin.k/modules {module-name manifest-address-or-nil}` (UCF section 7.6.4 form): the lift keeps the registry entry's `:address` for every registry-answered namespaced free name that discharge! answers via the registry (rows.cljc ~:1615-1617; a host-registered module has no address: nil, satisfied only by a host module of that name with equal export profiles via module/host-export-profile). Update the row grammar tables (docs/design/yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md section 5.x, UCF 7.6.4/7.6.5 pointers), the row encoder/decoder and validators, restore. Packs re-mint: regenerate test/resources/yin/vm/ucf/rows-checkpoint-v3.txt via the existing rows-checkpoint-fixtures/render route (see how 9ab9e792 did it) and record a dated entry in docs/design/yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md (I-8); no backward compatibility is owed. (2) LOWER re-check (B): `check-dependencies!` (rows.cljc ~:1898) re-discharges registry-answered names against the RECEIVER's registry by EQUAL ADDRESS (not name presence): a missing or different module refuses BEFORE attach with the exact outcome of section 4.2 (`:yin.k/unsatisfied`, `:yin.k/discovery :complete`, `:yin.k/missing {:yin.k/modules {...} :obligations #{...}}`), kind `:module-pin-mismatch` naming both addresses when the receiver holds a different address (words of engine.cljc:1388-1393 `:dependency-pin-mismatch`). The lower stays pure over the receiver value and attaches nothing on refusal (attach-count law); the receiver's registry is still kept as given. (3) R4: carried `:install` children: the lower refuses a child unless its manifest address is in a composition-supplied opts set `{:yin.k/admitted {name address}}` (default empty = fail closed), as `:yin.k/unsatisfied {:yin.k/missing {:yin.k/modules {name carried-address}}}` before any attach (section 4.4); and at `link-install` (engine.cljc ~:1436-1443) the copied sender `:admission` record must not stand for the receiver's decision: replace it by the receiver's (opts-supplied) record or drop it, as the report specifies. (4) Documentation: continuation 2.5 and 7.2 (the lower now re-discharges registry names by pinned address; Q5 answered C), UCF 7.11, the refusal shape, and the FORBIDDEN list for a composition's fetch loop (section 4.2 last bullet, section 5) in the right design doc; update docs/agents/known-gaps.md rows (Q5, R4 install-child admission). The fetch LOOP itself is NOT part of this slice (composition policy; no fetch code in the VM or lower; do not add one). TESTS (portable .cljc, section 7.1): pin equal-address satisfaction, different-address refusal naming both addresses, missing-module refusal before attach with attach-count zero, host-module nil pin with equal and unequal profiles, install child refused with empty admitted set and accepted when listed, `link-install` no longer copies the sender's admission, the decoded p