{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '192,225p' collab/1793520000000-architect-fetch-threat-model.report.md; sed -n '2080,2130p' src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc; sed -n '2180,2290p' src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc; rg -n 'install|admission|lower-task' test/yin/vm/ucf/rows_test.cljc | tail -45; rg -n 'install|lower-task|opts' test/yin/vm/semantic/safepoint_harness_test.cljc | tail -35\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '192,225p' collab/1793520000000-architect-fetch-threat-model.report.md; sed -n '2080,2130p' src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc; sed -n '2180,2290p' src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/rows.cljc; rg -n 'install|admission|lower-task' test/yin/vm/ucf/rows_test.cljc | tail -45; rg -n 'install|lower-task|opts' test/yin/vm/semantic/safepoint_harness_test.cljc | tail -35\"","aggregated_output":"## 5. What must NOT live in the VM or the lower (D confirmed rejected)\n\n- **No fetch in `resolve-var`.** It would make every `:var` instruction an\n  implicit network operation (invariants: no implicit control flow, callbacks\n  are stream events; I4 no operation waits, `yin.vm.linker.md:179-182`; I6 the\n  VM never invokes a loader, `:196-199`). The custody gate stops link\n  requests under `:exporting` (`module.cljc:541-543`); a resolve-time fetch\n  would have to re-invent that discipline inside the evaluator.\n- **No admission context in the VM.** \"Who is asking\" is composition-owned\n  holder context, never a datum (`yin.vm.linker.dht.md:2248-2255`); the VM\n  has none to give.\n- **No clock, no lease, no budget in the lower.** The lower is pure and\n  portable; liveness is `dao.lease`'s and the drive's (`linker.cljc:1958-1960`).\n- **No name environment or trust in the carrier.** A pack may pin an address\n  (a fact of S's state); it may not assert who may bind a name (a pinned\n  address \"is never a name claim\", `yin.vm.linker.dht.md:1835-1837`).\n- **No registry entries in the row table.** Code travels as segments; a\n  module's installed slice does not travel (continuation §2.5 `:360-366`\n  stands); only the binding fact `name → address` travels.\n- **No language, frontend or session key** anywhere in the new shape\n  (`yin.vm.linker.dht.md:2302-2316`).\n\n## 6. Verdict on Q5\n\n**C**, implemented as B plus one map, in UCF's already-specified shape.\n\n- **A is unacceptable.** It has the only runtime symptom in the gap list\n  (`collab/1793430000000-architect-gap-list.report.md:125`), it fails\n  **after** effects under R's authority (R8), and it hides version skew (R1,\n  R6) completely.\n- **B alone is insufficient.** Refusing before attach fixes R8 but keeps\n  name-only satisfaction, so dependency confusion (R1), skew (R6) and the\n  TOCTOU on name presence (R5) remain, and a fetch loop driven by names\n  gives M1 a free hand to choose what R loads (R2) subject only to R's trust\n                                    :ancestry (conj (vec (:ancestry recv)) mn)\n                                    :capability-secret (when (fn? source) (source origin))})]\n    [(cond-> (dissoc child :yin.k/closes :yin.k/issued :yin.k/gate :yin.k/custody\n                     :yin.k/recovery-waits :yin.k/recovery-parked :yin.k/recovery-cell-ids)\n       fenced? (assoc :make-stream (:make-stream recv)))\n     (assoc recv :origins (inc n))]))\n\n\n(defn- restore-task\n  \"Step 12 for one task: code by A, fresh resource keys, values re-sealed\n   under recv, waits as engine entries, parked records, installs, and the\n   custody check-custody! answered (with-custody).\"\n  [recv task handles custody root?]\n  (let [[_ _ kind _ id-counter free-env store module-stores parked census _ code installs waits parked-id result]\n        (:slots task)\n        base (reduce (fn [r [_ v]] (module/attach-module r v))\n                     (assoc (dissoc recv :yin.k/closes :yin.k/issued :yin.k/gate :yin.k/custody\n                                    :yin.k/recovery-waits :yin.k/recovery-parked :yin.k/recovery-cell-ids)\n                            :code {} :code-aliases {} :program nil)\n                     (sort-by #(str (key %)) code))\n        aliases (:code-aliases base)\n        used (atom (into fixed-resource-keys (keys (:resources base))))\n        identities (sort-by str (distinct (map #(first (:slots %)) (rows-of task :stream true))))\n        stream-keys (into {} (map (fn [identity] [identity (fresh-key! used)])) identities)\n        pairs (mapv vec (partition 2 (:slots census)))\n        cell-keys (into {} (map (fn [[c _]] [c (fresh-key! used)])) pairs)\n        bodies (into {} pairs)\n        stream-key #(get stream-keys (first (:slots %)))\n        parked-index (into {} (map vec) (partition 2 (:slots parked)))\n        cache (atom {})\n        resolving (atom #{})]\n    (letfn [(value\n              [v]\n              (case (first v)\n                :lit (second v)\n                :cursor-cell (engine/issue-ref base :cursor-ref (get cell-keys (second v)))\n                :row (row (second v))))\n            (built\n              [n coll expected]\n              (when (< (count coll) expected)\n                ;; Re-emit only on refusal to recover the decoded row's address.\n                (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :host-collapse\n                          {:yin.k/path [(first (emit-node n {} {}))]}))\n              coll)\n            (row\n              [n]\n              (let [ss (:slots n)]\n                (case (:kind n)\n                  :vec (mapv value ss)\n                  :list (apply list (map value ss))\n                  :set (built n (into #{} (map value) ss) (count ss))\n              [w]\n              (let [[state pending] (:slots w)\n                    [reason & xs] (:slots pending)\n                    p (payload state)]\n                (case reason\n                  :next (assoc p :reason :next :stream-id (cell-stream (first xs))\n                               :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref :id (get cell-keys (first xs))})\n                  :ffi (let [[c call-id op] xs]\n                         (cond-> (assoc p :reason :next :stream-id (cell-stream c) :call-id call-id\n                                        :cursor-ref {:type :cursor-ref :id (get cell-keys c)})\n                           (some? op) (assoc :op op)))\n                  :put (let [[s v op-id] xs]\n                         (cond-> (assoc p :reason :put :stream-id (stream-key s) :datom (value v))\n                           (some? op-id) (assoc :op-id op-id)))\n                  :ffi-request (let [[call-id envelope req resp c op-id] xs\n                                     datom (value envelope)]\n                                 (cond-> (assoc p :reason :put :stream-id (stream-key req) :datom datom\n                                                :request-sent true :call-id call-id :op (apply2/request-op datom)\n                                                :response-cursor (get cell-keys c) :response-stream (stream-key resp))\n                                   (some? op-id) (assoc :op-id op-id)))\n                  (:link-request :link-response)\n                  (let [[link-id mn _ _ c] xs\n                        [envelope op-id] (when (= :link-request reason) (drop 5 xs))]\n                    (cond-> (assoc p :reason reason :link-id link-id :name mn\n                                   :request module/link-request-resource :response module/link-response-resource\n                                   :try? (last xs) :cursor (second (:slots (get bodies c))))\n                      (= :link-request reason) (assoc :envelope envelope)\n                      (some? op-id) (assoc :op-id op-id)))\n                  :install (assoc p :reason :install :name (first xs) :try? (second xs)))))]\n      (let [store' (reduce (fn [s [k v]] (engine/store-put s k (value v))) {} (partition 2 (:slots store)))\n            stores (into {} (map (fn [ms]\n                                   (let [[mid s] (:slots ms)]\n                                     [mid (into {} (map (fn [[k v]] [k (value v)])) (partition 2 (:slots s)))])))\n                         module-stores)\n            parked' (into {} (map (fn [[p _]] [p (parked-record p)])) parked-index)\n            entries (mapv entry waits)\n            link (some #(let [[reason _ _ req resp] (:slots (second (:slots %)))]\n                          (when (contains? #{:link-request :link-response} reason) [req resp]))\n                       waits)\n            [base installs'] (reduce (fn [[r acc] inst]\n                                       (let [[mn phase parent response child] (:slots inst)\n                                             [spawned r'] (spawn-child r response mn (:fenced? custody))]\n                                         [r' (assoc acc mn {:phase phase :parent parent :response response\n                                                            :vm (restore-task spawned child handles custody false)})]))\n                                     [base {}] installs)\n            fe (keyed free-env)\n            resources (merge (:resources base)\n                             (into {} (map (fn [[identity k]] [k (get handles identity)])) stream-keys)\n                             (into {} (map (fn [[c body]]\n                                             [(get cell-keys c) {:stream-id (stream-key (first (:slots body)))\n                                                                 :cursor (second (:slots body))}]))\n                                   pairs)\n                             (when-let [[req resp] link]\n                               {module/link-request-resource (get handles (first (:slots req)))\n                                module/link-response-resource (get handles (first (:slots resp)))}))\n            ;; a fenced rehydration carries the counter exactly, so the\n            ;; relift reproduces the published root; a resumption adopts\n            ;; max(local, carried)\n            machine (cond-> (assoc base :store store' :module-stores stores :parked parked' :installs installs'\n                                   :resources resources :env fe :free-env fe :window {} :k nil :control nil\n                                   :ready-queue []\n                                   :id-counter (if (:fenced? custody)\n                                                 id-counter\n                                                 (max (or (:id-counter base) 0) id-counter)))\n                      ;; resource key -> the carrier's cursor cell, so one\n                      ;; cell is one key and two cells two (UCF 7.7.4)\n                      (:fenced? custody)\n                      (assoc :yin.k/recovery-cell-ids (into {} (map (fn [[c k]] [k c])) cell-keys)))]\n        (with-custody\n          (case kind\n            :halted (assoc machine :halted? true :blocked? false :value (value result) :wait-set [])\n            :parked (assoc machine :halted? true :blocked? false :value (get parked' parked-id) :wait-set entries)\n            (assoc machine :halted? false :blocked? true :value :yin/blocked :wait-set entries))\n          custody kind root?)))))\n\n\n(defn lower-task\n  \"The lower of §7.2 into recv, a fresh semantic machine of the\n   receiver's composition: gate to frames (decode) and the store keys,\n   then pendings and install records, dependency closure (code, closures,\n   primitives), each step over the whole tree before the next, then\n   custody (check-custody!), all before the first attach! (step 11); then\n   restore (step 12), which therefore meets no carrier defect. Answers the\n   restored machine, or throws the first refusal as ex-data.\n   opts: :budget; :exclusive, refuse a fork root; :grant and :protection,\n   required by a blocked or parked exclusive root (handoff.cljc's reader\n   contract: the grant names :checkpoint, the pack address, its lease,\n   holder, tenure and evidence; :protection maps every stream identity of\n   the tree to its class); :fenced, an administrative rehydration that\n   skips the grant and restores every task of the tree gated :exporting,\n   its waits in :yin.k/recovery-waits and its parked records in\n   :yin.k/recovery-parked (none in the scheduler), its id counter the\n   carried one exactly and :yin.k/recovery-cell-ids mapping each cursor\n   cell's resource key to its carried cell id.\"\n  ([recv wire attach!] (lower-task recv wire attach! {}))\n  ([recv wire attach! opts]\n   (let [task (decode wire (merge default-budget (:budget opts)))]\n     (when-not (= :task (:kind task)) (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :root {}))\n     ;; each step over the whole tree before the next (§3.3)\n     (doseq [step [check-stores! check-pendings! check-dependencies!]\n             [t role] (task-tree task :root)]\n       (step recv t role))\n     (let [custody (check-custody! task wire opts)]\n       (restore-task recv task (attach-streams! attach! task) custody true)))))\n235:                                                    [(rows/node :install ['a :running nil {} child])])))\n238:                         (fn [rs] (mapv #(if (= :install (second %)) (assoc % 6 root) %) rs)))]\n295:        parent (rows/node :task (assoc (:slots root) 12 [(rows/node :install ['a :running nil {} child])\n296:                                                         (rows/node :install ['b :running nil {} child])]))\n375:   install children included.\"\n405:  \"Source ids of every census in the tree, install children included.\"\n486:  \"parent with one install 'a holding child (slot 3 set to :child).\"\n489:                          [(rows/node :install ['a :running nil {} (rows/node :task (assoc (:slots child) 3 :child))])])))\n784:  ;; An install child's refusal names the install; decode prefixes the root.\n944:  \"A parent with two installs of one random child task.\"\n948:    (rows/node :task (assoc (:slots parent) 12 [(rows/node :install ['a :running nil {} child])\n949:                                                (rows/node :install ['b :running nil {} child])]))))\n1050:            refusal (error #(rows/lower-task\n1083:            restored (rows/lower-task (support/new-machine) pack (fn [_] nil))]\n1114:           [:install-child (support/parked-installer) [:installs 'host.mod :vm] 42]]]\n1117:            ;; Share attached handles so install records can be compared\n1132:            ;; A fixed composition key is already reserved by lower-task,\n1142:                             :installs (assoc {} 'receiver.mod {:phase :running})\n1146:            clean (rows/lower-task fresh pack attach!)\n1147:            restored (rows/lower-task populated pack attach!)\n1148:            fields [:code :store :module-stores :parked :installs :wait-set :ready-queue]\n1158:                        (rows/lower-task collision-receiver pack attach!))\n1165:          (is (not (contains? restored-task k)) (str k \" is absent in the install child too\")))\n1177:              (str field \" is isolated in the resumed task, including an install child\")))\n1181:        (is (not (contains? (:installs restored) 'receiver.mod)))\n1229:        m (rows/lower-task populated wire attach! opts)]\n1240:    (testing \"fenced restoration owns recovery data throughout an install tree\"\n1241:      (let [pack (support/lift (support/parked-installer) nil)\n1248:            clean (rows/lower-task fresh pack attach! {:fenced true})\n1249:            restored (rows/lower-task populated pack attach! {:fenced true})]\n1250:        (doseq [path [[] [:installs 'host.mod :vm]]]\n1269:          recv (rows/lower-task (support/new-machine) pack attach!)\n1279:          recv (rows/lower-task (support/new-machine) pack attach!)]\n1312:                   {:yin.k/reason :install :yin.k/name 'host.mod}]]\n1365:                (verdict (error #(rows/lower-task (support/new-machine) wire attach!)))))))\n1231:  (testing \"an install record (8) before the root's dependency closure (9)\"\n1232:    (is (= [:yin.k/undecodable :install-phase]\n1233:           (take 2 (refused-before-attach 10 (comp #(update-at % (conj install-path 1) (constantly :bogus))\n1254:        r (try (rows/lift-task m (fn [h] (swap! n inc) (serve! h)) (lift-opts))\n1318:        wire (rows/lift-task m serve! (lift-opts))\n1372:            wire (rows/lift-task (routed-beside-stream ast stores) serve! (lift-opts))\n1390:          wire (rows/lift-task m serve! (lift-opts))\n1409:          m (-> (scope m) (update-in [:installs 'host.mod :vm] scope))\n1411:          wire (rows/lift-task m serve! (lift-opts))\n1412:          child-path (conj install-path 4)\n1430:   and §4 defines no layout for install children (canonical-task refuses\n1431:   :installs). The reference lane runs the whole matrix; these lanes are\n1457:    (rows/lift-task m serve! (lift-opts))\n1458:    (layout/lift-task m (kernel-space m) (on-lane :semantic machine) serve! (lift-opts))))\n1462:  \"The lower of §7.2 into a fresh receiver on lane, of composition opts.\"\n1463:  [lane opts wire attach!]\n1464:  (let [scratch (on-lane :semantic #(machine opts))]\n1466:      (rows/lower-task scratch wire attach!)\n1467:      (layout/lower-task scratch (on-lane lane #(machine opts)) wire attach!))))\n1732:            recv (lane-lower to (merge {:attach-stream attach!} (:opts receiver)) wire attach!)\n1754:                d (error #(lane-lower to (merge {:attach-stream attach!} (:opts receiver)) wire attach!))]\n1944:              wire (rows/lift-task (:machine world) serve! (lift-opts))\n1984:(deftest install-return-contract-and-link-flag-validation\n1986:    (let [world (installing (try-wrapper try?) false nil)\n1988:          wire (rows/lift-task (:machine world) serve! (lift-opts))\n1991:          recv (rows/lower-task (machine) wire attach!)\n1992:          abandoned (engine/abandon-installs recv :test-abandoned)]\n1993:      (is (= [:install 'host.mod try?] (:slots pending)))\n2002:                 #(installing identity false nil)]\n2005:          wire (rows/lift-task (:machine (build)) serve! (lift-opts))\n2009:          result (error #(rows/lower-task (machine) bad (fn [_] (swap! attached inc))))]\n2020:        wire (rows/lift-task parked serve! (lift-opts))\n2022:        recv (rows/lower-task (machine {:attach-stream attach!}) wire attach!)\n2042:        wire (rows/lift-task m serve! (lift-opts))\n2045:        recv (rows/lower-task (machine {:attach-stream attach! :call-in own-in\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
