members; JVM verified, Node/Dart assigned to orchestrator | P2 |\n| dead fixture: `yin.vm.malformed-rows/malformed-vectors` (the v3 §7.5 vector rules) has no reader since the old vector validator died | 8g sweep | yin.vm.semantic (the register-VM track) | closed in follow-up-1: deleted after source/test reader search | P3 |\n| what died at phase 8, for the record: `yin.vm.completion` (its agreement facts survive in `semantic/scan_test`), and `yin.vm.ucf`'s v3 canonicalizer and stack-shaped safepoint halves (un-ported: completion in 8f-1, UCF halves in 8f-3; R2/R3; `yin.vm.ucf` is now only `code-address`) | 8f-1 ruling | yin.vm.semantic (the register-VM track) | recorded in 8g (`yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md` I-6, the dependency-completion banner, linker §5.2 note) | P3 |\n| Historical citations of `docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.md` with v3 section numbers, now wrong after the rename and outside the nine-line allowance: `src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:655` (§2), `src/cljc/datomworld/demo/continuation_handoff.cljc:67`, `src/cljs/datomworld/demo/continuation_stream.cljs:10` (§7), `src/cljd/yin/register_bench_cljd.cljd:6` (§8), `src/cljc/yin/vm/docs/jfr_benchmark_analysis.md:5,268` (§8), `test/bench/yin_vm_bench.cljc:3` (§8), `test/yin/repl_test.cljc:37` (§8), `test/yin/vm/semantic/linearize_test.cljc:286` (§2.7); in the renamed design §2 is the machine, §7 is \"What A is\", §8 is the derivations | 8g Architect review P2-1 | yin.vm.semantic (the register-VM track) | closed in follow-up-1: retargeted to the history block or current projection/cutover sections; only prose changed | P3 |\n| Historical source prose outside the nine citation-line allowance: the optimisation note mentions the deleted `vm/opcase`; `ucf/rows/checkpoint.cljc` says it replaces the now-deleted `yin.vm.ucf.checkpoint` | 8f-1 review D1 / P3-5 | yin.vm.semantic (the register-VM track) | closed in follow-up-1: optimisation note marks `vm/opcase` historical; rows inspector records deletion of the predecessor in 8f-1 | P3 |\n| Node `store-test` two-worker-threads flaky | quick and slow tiers | store | open | P3 |\n| Dart `dao.stream.datagram.dart-test/refusals-and-lifecycle-events` (Linux) | quick tier | dao.stream | open | P3 |\n| L-e (closure-origin and store-ownership verification) not implemented | docs 7.5 | linker | L-e | P1 |\n| DHT 64 KiB blob cap: `py` cannot travel over DHT | docs 7.5 | DHT seat | chunked transport | P2 |\n| CLI refusal for a bad `--dht-trust` value no longer names the flag (`main/parse-trust` could prefix it); shared parser docstring still says \"A `--dht-trust` value\" | fable AL-4-nits review P3-1 | yin.repl | next yin.repl slice | P3 |\n| `(untrust <own>)` says \"always trusted\" on an `:external` session, where the external admitter decides | fable AL-4-nits review P3-2 | yin.repl | next yin.repl slice | P3 |\n| Closed 2026-10-16: `:try?` carried by all three UCF link pending variants; lifted try waiters retain their return contract | G1 / L-d-1b slice: row/frame and remote lift/lower; portable refusal, install and malformed-boolean tests in `semantic/safepoint_harness_test.cljc`, frame bijection in `ucf/rows_test.cljc` | UCF | L-d-1b closed | P1 |\n| try joiner's `:link-id` is the install's parent id; drop `:link-id` from install waiters, loss datum carries `:module` | fable L-d-1 review P3-1 | linker | L-d-1b | P3 |\n| `publish/requirements` pins only operator `require`; module-level `try-require` yields no pin | fable L-d-1 review P3-3 | linker | closed in L-d-3 | P3 |\n| publication-time-unavailable optional imports cannot be represented without concrete segment pins | mob consensus I4 Q1 | yang.python / linker | open | P3 |\n| C4 scanner pins `[:c4 :py]` / `[:c4 :t]` in `test/yin/vm/semantic/scanner_goldens.cljc` stale since I4-a; slow `scan-test` bodies fail on master until regenerated | follow-up-1 / owner scheduling | yang.python seat / muse | open: regenerate once at the end of I5/I6 with Architect review | P2 |\n| lower `keyed` builder (`ucf/rows.cljc`, ~:2135-2137: `:bindings`, `:store`, `:window` and cursor-cell census rows) has no `built`-style host-collapse guard for identifier keys: on JS two slash-crossed symbols (`(symbol \"a/b\" \"c\")` vs `(symbol \"a\" \"b/c\")`) as binding names merge in the host map; hand-crafted carrier only (the reader cannot produce such symbols and `:slot-kind` does not split on `/`); decode already refuses the numeric `equiv` collapses | follow-up-1 round-2 Architect confirm P3 | yin.vm.semantic (the register-VM track) | open: mirror the `built` count guard in `keyed`, one test on Node (JS-only case) | P3 |\n3837:   through its carried descriptor. Missing/gone routes or profiles yield\n3840:   seed it with the carried position without calling `cursor` on an\n3877:  install or call evidence refuses without publishing a partial body.\n3940:install child cannot keep stepping. Freeze the entire task and its child\n3980:restarts from its carried sequence; a successor carries the next sequence.\n4031:  install child.\n4040:- A carried id names the occurrence it was assigned under. Admission\n4075:install children, an enrolled target without an operation id refuses\n4185:  and tick its install child. Assert: one admitted holder; competitors\n4279:gets no reply. A carried proposal or release answers `{:yin.k/status\n4280::carried}`; the judge's answer to it is learned from the ledger, through\n4283:be named or does not take the append answers `:suspended :uncarried`.\n4285:or release is not carried and answers `:suspended :unavailable`. A lost\n4310:   outcomes. If the approved explicit-park or complete install-child shape\n4311:   is absent, amend UCF 7.4.3 first; never export the name-only install\n4312:   sketch as complete task state. Update 7.11's evidence pointers without\n4315:   and the version-1 block of 7.11.1. Both 7.4.3 shapes were absent\n4325:   Wire `yin.repl.core`'s handoff composition as UCF 7.11 requires; keep\n4350:- `validate-body` validates the install en