{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\np='test/yin/vm/semantic/safepoint_harness_test.cljc';s=open(p).read();lines=s.splitlines(True);keep={569,743,888,1148,1472,1997};s=''.join(l.replace('wire attach\"'! install-lower-opts)'\"', 'wire attach\"'!)'\"') if i not in keep else l for i,l in enumerate(lines,1));open(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\nsed -n '2317,2343p' docs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.md; sed -n '2854,2875p' docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md; tail -12 /tmp/module-pins-focused.log\"","aggregated_output":"#### 7.5.11 Exposure: the registry and its installation family\n\nAdmission governs entry into a registry. An allow admits one address\ninto the requesting task's registry, and authorization follows that\nregistry and its installation-family inheritance:\n\n- `link-install` spawns the install child over the parent's linked\n  entries and receives each into it;\n- the child's installs transfer back to the parent with their\n  `:admission` record;\n- a name already resolvable in the registry answers with no link request\n  and hence no question.\n\nThe exposure domain is therefore the installation family for its life,\nnot one task. It is about principal plus address plus holder context,\nand it is language-blind: any frontend compiling to a require of that\nname hits the same entry.\n\n- **Untrust is not retroactive.** `(untrust p)` changes the decision\n  snapshot for questions not yet answered. It evicts no registry entry,\n  revokes no appended response, and leaves a question already answered\n  allow allowed.\n- `(reset)` and `(vm ...)` start a fresh registry and a fresh admission\n  state.\n\n#### 7.5.12 Trust versus safety\n\n## §7.11 Acceptance blockers for the implementation phase\n\nThe warning at the top of this file is retained until each of these is\nclosed with a test in the parity or conformance suite. The first four are\nthe review's named architectural obligations; they are blockers to\n*accepting the design*, not merely work items.\n\n- **Authority grounding and wiring.** The arbitration `dao.space`, its\n  transactor as grantor, the occurrence ledger with epochs, and the\n  attribution resolver `dao.lease.md` requires, are composition duties; the\n  first composition to ship UCF is `yin.repl.core`'s handoff demo, and\n  its wiring becomes the worked example. A composition without a\n  transactable space offers `:yin.k/fork` only.\n- **Execution identity.** Occurrence minting, the `:yin.k/origin` chain,\n  retry idempotence (one occurrence per park), and successor completion as\n  a grantor ledger transition need conformance tests, including the crash\n  windows of §7.7.5.\n- **Pending-state completeness.** Every pending variant of §7.4.3 must\n  round-trip and resume *elsewhere*: retained writes, sent and retained FFI\n  calls with both endpoints and the kept response cursor, and cursor cells\n  through the aliasing scenarios of `check-wait-set`. This depends on\n  `dao.stream.remote.md` and its **portable cursor profile**\nFAIL in (install-children-lower-under-their-roots-custody) (rows_custody_test.cljc:342)\nexpected: (= :running (:yin.k/gate child))\n  actual: (not (= :running nil))\n\nFAIL in (install-children-lower-under-their-roots-custody) (rows_custody_test.cljc:344)\nexpected: (= [(s/op-id 4)] (keep :op-id (:wait-set child)))\n  actual: (not (= [#:yin.k{:occurrence \"1d3e5b7a-0c2f-4a69-8b11-7e6d5c4b3a02\", :seq 4}] ()))\n\nFAIL in (the-grammar-runs-before-any-attachment) (rows_custody_test.cljc:234)\nchild-header\nexpected: (= (select-keys (f/refusal n) [:yin.k/status :yin.k/kind :yin.k/path]) (select-keys (refused (f/pack-of n) (exclusive-opts (f/pack-of n) #{\"s0\"})) [:yin.k/status :yin.k/kind :yin.k/path]))\n  actual: (not (= #:yin.k{:status :yin.k/undecodable, :kind :child-header, :path [:installs host.mod :custody]} #:yin.k{:status :yin.k/unsatisfied}))\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
