{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_33","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"python3 - <<'PY'\np='docs/design/yin.vm.semantic.continuation.md';s=open(p).read();anchor='Then **attachment** (step 11, \"'`attach-streams!`):'\"';s=s.replace(anchor,'''**Amended 2026-10-16 (module-pins, R4).** After custody validation and\nbefore attachment, every carried install child must have its manifest\naddress listed under its module name in the receiving composition's\n\"'`opts {:yin.k/admitted {name manifest-address}}`. The default is empty:\nan absent or different address refuses as\n`{:yin.k/status :yin.k/unsatisfied\n  :yin.k/missing {:yin.k/modules {name carried-address}}}`.\nThis applies to children throughout the task tree, including fenced\nrestoration. Restore drops the sender'\"'s \"'`:yin.admit/id`, `:yin.admit/decision`,\n`:yin.admit/asserters` and `:yin.admit/address` from each retained install\nresponse before `link-install` can record them as receiver evidence. The\ncomposition supplies admissions from its own policy, never from the pack.\n\n'\"'''+anchor);s=s.replace('This verifies response self-consistency; binding to composition-known\\\\n  content addresses remains the linker\\\\'s fetch/admission responsibility.', '''This verifies response self-consistency. Amended 2026-10-16 (R4): the\n  lower additionally requires the receiver composition's explicit\n  \"'`:yin.k/admitted {name manifest-address}` before attaching any stream,\n  and drops the sender'\"'s admission evidence on restore.''');open(p,'w').write(s)\np='docs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.md';s=open(p).read();anchor='The exposure domain is therefore the installation family for its life,';s=s.replace(anchor,'''**Amended 2026-10-16 (carried install children, R4).** A lowered pack's\ninstall child enters this family only when the receiving composition\nexplicitly admits its name and manifest address through lower opts\n\"'`:yin.k/admitted`. The lower refuses unlisted or differently addressed\nchildren before any stream attachment, including during fenced restore.\nSender admission fields are dropped from the retained response; they do\nnot become the receiving registry entry'\"'s \"'`:admission`.\n\n'\"'''+anchor);open(p,'w').write(s)\np='docs/design/yin.vm.universal-continuation-format.md';s=open(p).read();anchor='- **Execution identity.**';s=s.replace(anchor,'''- **Receiver module satisfaction and install admission (2026-10-16).**\n  Architect verdict C requires registry bindings pinned by manifest address\n  (§7.6.4/§7.6.5) and receiver re-discharge before attachment. The module-pin\n  carrier work is blocked pending the host-export-profile slot/schema\n  decision; do not treat name presence as equal-address satisfaction.\n  Carried install admission (R4) is implemented by the lower's explicit\n  \"'`:yin.k/admitted {name manifest-address}` option, default empty, and\n  sender admission evidence is dropped on restore. The fetch loop remains\n  composition work: fetch before the grant proposal (14.2.3 step 2), retry\n  the same pack bytes, at most one require per missing module and two\n  lowers per attempt, under a per-run lease. The loop is **forbidden** to\n  seed `:name-env` from the carrier, switch derivation to `:trusted`, pass\n  carrier-named `:fallback` formats, or require names outside the reported\n  `:yin.k/modules`. No fetch, clock, lease or admission policy belongs in\n  the VM, `resolve-var` or the pure lower.\n'\"'''+anchor,1);open(p,'w').write(s)\np='docs/agents/known-gaps.md';s=open(p).read();s+='''| Q5: receiver accepts registry dependencies by name only; Architect verdict C requires module identity pins and receiver re-discharge | fetch threat model §4.2, §6; engineer module-pins stopped on unspecified host-profile carrier slot/schema | VM Runtime / Architect | blocked: host-profile carrier decision; module pins not implemented | P1 |\n| R4: carried install child bypasses receiver admission and carries sender evidence | fetch threat model §4.4 | VM Runtime | implemented uncommitted 2026-10-16: explicit \"'`:yin.k/admitted` name/address gate before attach; sender admission dropped on restore; pending Architect review | P1 |\n| Composition fetch loop per-run lease and budget absent | fetch threat model §4.3; reserved `:lease` policy | composition | outside module-pins slice; no fetch loop added | P2 |\n'\"''';open(p,'w').write(s)\np='docs/design/yin.vm.ucf-revisions.md';s=open(p).read();s+='''\n**2026-10-16, I-8 (module-pins slice, partial; R4 only).** Lower now\nrequires composition-supplied \"'`:yin.k/admitted {name manifest-address}`\nfor every carried install child, default empty, before attaching streams;\nrestore drops the sender'\"'s admission decision fields. No row shape or\nfixture address changes in this partial slice. The module-pin carrier,\nhost-profile schema and their fixture re-mint are blocked pending the\nArchitect's decision on where host-module export profiles are recorded.\nNo compatibility promise is added.\n''';open(p,'w').write(s)\nPY\ntail -8 /tmp/module-pins-focused.log\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
