{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_57","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'install|requires|admission' docs/design/yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md | head -28; sed -n '122,150p' docs/design/yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md; tail -10 /tmp/module-pins-quick-unrestricted.log\"","aggregated_output":"99:id to one row. The gate's walk over install children follows only\n100:`:install` child crefs and keeps an **active recursion-path set**: a\n103:*off* the active path is not an error: two install entries whose\n106:DAG, and each install entry still restores as its own native task\n122:default, and a later Jing default requires another carrier version,\n158:root and per install child.\n171:  `:install` pending names a module whose entry holds a child body.\n233:§7.4.3 requires to be in the canonical-bytes domain but that are not\n234:guest literals and contain no guest values, namely install responses,\n237:governs it (an install response by the linker's delivery checks, an\n269:`:parked-table`, `:cursor-cells`, the installs and module-stores slots) must\n285:| `:prim` | `name-S` | the named primitive after the profile check (UCF §7.5.2); the profile lives in requires |\n291:§6 requires and lower differently: a reified value becomes a\n338:| `:install` | `name-S  try?-D` |\n356:An `:install` pending is never sufficient alone: the root's installs\n358:`:yin.k/non-portable` kind `:incomplete-install` and a body carrying it\n368:| `:install` | `name-S  phase  parent-D  response-D  child-cref` |\n383:parked record (continuation §2.5). An `:install` row carries the complete\n388:requires receiver verification, never trust merely because it decodes:\n394:**Amended after 7 (2026-10-14)** — Reason: 7b enforces install link and manifest/image agreement at lower.\n395:The merged lower (`rows/check-install!`) verifies, before any attachment:\n396:the phase is one of `#{:running :parked}` (`:install-phase`); the\n400:receiving kernel's loader admits (`:install-response`); and the carried\n401:child task's kind is `:blocked` (`:install-child`), the only kind the\n404:but the engine never exposes at a safepoint). Lower also requires\n405:non-nil `parent` equal to response `:yin.link/id` (`:install-link-id`).\n409:hash-identify the image's `:value` vector (`:install-image`). These are\n411:admission path binds code and trees to composition-known addresses.\ndefault, and a later Jing default requires another carrier version,\nexactly as it would for A. Version-3 verification and re-emission (§6,\n§8) always use BLAKE3, whatever the reader's default is at the time;\nthis matters because root body bytes contain child-row addresses, so\nthe numbering procedure's leaf keys depend on the digest and are\ncanonical *within* a carrier version. **Amended after 7 (2026-10-14)** — Addresses are self-describing (`:segment/blake3-…`, `:segment/sha256-…`); before digest verification and numbering, a reader refuses a parsed non-BLAKE3 row id as `:yin.k/undecodable :row-algorithm`, then verifies each remaining id under the algorithm its address names, refusing a malformed id or digest mismatch as `:yin.k/hash-mismatch :row`.\nEqual bodies are one row. The id is Merkle: it\ncommits to every row id in the body.\n\n**Identity rows** are cursor cells (UCF §7.5.3, \"Terminology: cursor,\ncursor cell, cursor-ref, cell\", which defines all four words; this document\nuses them exactly as defined there). Before 2026-10-12 this document called\nthe cursor cell a \"cell\" and spelled its tags `:cells`, `:cell-body`,\n`[:cell C]`, `:yin.k/c-<n>`; the version-2 handoff carrier keeps those\nspellings. A cursor cell has a task-local id `C`\nin the form `:yin.k/cc-<n>`, minted by the lift under §6's canonical\nnumbering (the n-th cursor cell met in §6's canonical walk), never content-addressed, and scoped to the task whose root\ncarries it: a cursor-cell id means nothing outside its root, in a pool or a\nquery, and two tasks' `:yin.k/cc-1` are unrelated.\n\n**The census.** A cursor cell's *contents* (its stream marker and kept position)\nare not reachable through its id, so a content row that references a\ncursor cell commits to the cursor cell's identity but not to what the cursor cell holds. The\nroot therefore carries a **cursor-cell census**, a content row\n\n```clojure\n[X :cursor-cells  C₁ B₁  C₂ B₂  …]          ; sorted by n; Bᵢ is a cref\n[Bᵢ :cursor-cell-body  stream-cref  position]\n```\n\nTesting dao.postgraphics.packing-test\n\nTesting dao.postgraphics.raster-test\n\nTesting dao.postgraphics.terminal-test\n\nTesting dao.pretty-test\n\nTesting dao.space.dht-test\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
